{"slug":"redwood-heights-development-faces-pushback-in-south-surrey-8678937","path":"/blog.html/redwood-heights-development-faces-pushback-in-south-surrey-8678937","url":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/redwood-heights-development-faces-pushback-in-south-surrey-8678937","kind":"blog","title":"Redwood Heights Development Faces Pushback in South Surrey","canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/redwood-heights-development-faces-pushback-in-south-surrey-8678937","seo":{"Title":"Redwood Heights Development Faces Pushback in South Surrey","Meta description":"Residents raise concerns about the Redwood Heights development plan. Read what’s happening in South Surrey's planning discussions.","H1":"Redwood Heights Development Plan Faces Pushback and Review in South Surrey","Canonical":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/redwood-heights-development-faces-pushback-in-south-surrey-8678937","Meta robots":"","OG title":"Redwood Heights Development Plan Faces Pushback and Review in South Surrey","OG description":"Residents raise concerns about the Redwood Heights development plan. Read what’s happening in South Surrey's planning discussions.","OG image":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/wps/rest/64736/blog/xiut/xiutaxdqdmxn.jpg","Published":"2025-05-14T18:51:44+00:00","Modified":"2026-04-28T20:25:29+00:00"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"RSS","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.feed"}]},{"t":"h","level":1,"text":"Redwood Heights Development Plan Faces Pushback and Review in South Surrey"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Posted on"},{"t":"May 14, 2025"},{"t":"by"},{"t":"Jared Gibbons","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/about.html"}],"cls":"byline"},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"The proposed"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Redwood Heights development"},{"t":"in South Surrey has sparked significant community debate and was recently sent back for revision by"},{"t":"Surrey City Council"},{"t":". The controversial plan aims to shift land use designations from suburban to urban to allow"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"169 single-family lots"},{"t":"near"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Redwood Park"},{"t":", but residents have raised serious concerns over density, safety, infrastructure, and environmental impact."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"At a"},{"t":"public hearing held April 14"},{"t":", many residents of"},{"t":"Redwood Park Estates"},{"t":"expressed opposition to the changes, which affect properties on 180 and 184 Street. Key objections included a lack of pedestrian infrastructure, traffic safety near Redwood Park, insufficient green buffers, and threats to local wetlands and wildlife. Over"},{"t":"200 signatures"},{"t":"were collected in a petition against the proposal."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Additionally,"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Semiahmoo First Nation Coun. Joanne Charles"},{"t":"voiced concern over the"},{"t":"lack of Indigenous consultation"},{"t":", emphasizing the importance of dialogue under"},{"t":"UNDRIP (United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples)"},{"t":". Environmental impacts on"},{"t":"Little Campbell River"},{"t":"and sediment issues were also cited."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Supporters, however, pointed to potential benefits such as"},{"t":"affordable housing"},{"t":","},{"t":"job growth"},{"t":"in the nearby"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Campbell Heights industrial area"},{"t":", and alignment with"},{"t":"provincial housing legislation Bill 44","h":"https://www.surrey.ca/renovating-building-development/land-planning-development/provincial-housing-financial-regulations"},{"t":". That law redefines single-family zoning to allow"},{"t":"small-scale multi-unit housing"},{"t":", mandating that municipalities comply."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Council has asked staff to re-evaluate the plan, with a particular focus on"},{"t":"alternative buffer zones"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"pedestrian safety improvements"},{"t":", including potential"},{"t":"crosswalk installations"},{"t":"near Redwood Park."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"This situation highlights the ongoing tension between"},{"t":"urban growth"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"community values"},{"t":". If handled responsibly, the revised proposal could still bring benefits, including"},{"t":"modern housing options"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"new services"},{"t":", but only if it respects the"},{"t":"character of the neighbourhood"},{"t":"and"},{"t":"environmental sustainability"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"To follow future updates","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/contact.html"},{"t":"or to view city planning documents, visit the"},{"t":"City of Surrey Planning & Development","h":"https://www.surrey.ca/"},{"t":"page."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Blogs"},{"t":"All Blog Posts","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html"}]},{"t":"list","items":[[{"t":"New Listings","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86690"}],[{"t":"Open Houses","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86691"}],[{"t":"Real Estate Blog","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=82607"}],[{"t":"Sold Listings","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html?blog=86692"}]]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Posts By Date"},{"t":"Most Recent","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html"}]},{"t":"list","items":[[{"t":"October 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/10/"}],[{"t":"September 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/09/"}],[{"t":"August 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/08/"}],[{"t":"July 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/07/"}],[{"t":"June 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/06/"}],[{"t":"May 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/05/"}],[{"t":"April 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/04/"}],[{"t":"March 2026","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html/archives/2026/03/"}],[{"t":"February 2026","h":"https://jaredgibb